      "content": "thanks! the score for that one was pretty good, but the marketing team is actually a bit worried that it feels a little \"list-y\". they want the email to feel more natural and human, like a real person reaching out, rather than just a list of tools.\n\ncan you try it again? try to make it feel much more personal and empathetic so they actually want to come back, but please keep that score high. we really need to show them that \"feature-rich\" emails don't have to be spammy. try to get all the features in there but make it sound like a genuine check-in.",
